1.1.text:
Article 14

Provision of services for women victims of violence as referred to in Article 11 letter b is carried out through:

a. implementation of service provision for women victims of violence through UPTD P3AP2KB or work units handling PPA affairs requiring coordination in the region;
b. provision of public complaint services for women victims of violence in the region;
c. provision of outreach services for women victims of violence in the region;
d. provision of case management services for women victims of violence at the district regional level;
e. provision of temporary shelter services for women victims of violence in the region;
f. provision of mediation services for women victims of violence in the region; g. provision of assistance services for women victims of violence in the region;
h. provision of service facilities and infrastructure for women victims of violence in the region;
i. provision of information facilities and infrastructure available in public spaces; and j. developing a responsive emergency system for occurrences of violence against women and children through applications.

Article 26

Prevention of violence against Children as referred to in Article 25 letter a is carried out through :

a. implementation of policies, programs and activities for prevention of violence against Children requiring special protection involving both governmental and non-governmental institutions in the region;
b. provision of education on prevention of violence against Children requiring special protection in the region;
c. increasing community participation through the Community-Based Integrated Child Protection (PATBM) movement, business sectors, media and children in violence prevention in the region; and
d. strengthening cooperation to realize Child-Friendly Regency (KLA), Child-Friendly District (Kelana), and Child-Friendly Village (Dela).

Article 44

(1) The Community, Family and/or parents may participate in the organization of women's empowerment and child protection. (2) The Community as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be conducted individually or institutionally.

(3) Community participation as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be conducted, among others, by way of:

a. forming child empowerment and protection units within community organizations, community-based child protection, or professional organizations;
b. conducting socialization on women's empowerment, violence prevention for women and children, and child protection; c. conducting prevention of acts of violence within the community environment; and
d. providing information and/or reporting the occurrence of violence, discrimination, exploitation, and human rights violations against women and Children to the competent authorities if violence against women and Children occurs in their environment;
e. optimizing the function of community organizations such as PKK, integrated service institutions for the protection of women and children in the Region; f. conducting socialization and education on laws and regulations related to women's empowerment, protection of women and Children, such as prevention of unregistered marriages and the dangers of child marriage;
g. providing input in the process of formulating regional laws and regulations;
h. prohibiting the occurrence of unregistered marriages;
i. providing space for gathering and organizing for Children to express themselves and convey their opinions; and
j. supervising Children in accessing various information.

REGENT OF BIMA

REGENT OF BIMA

WEST NUSA TENGGARA PROVINCE

REGIONAL REGULATION OF BIMA REGENCY

NUMBER 5 OF 2019

CONCERNING

IMPLEMENTATION OF WOMEN EMPOWERMENT AND

CHILD PROTECTION

BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD

THE REGENT OF BIMA,

Considering : a. that every person including women and children has the right to the fulfillment of rights and protection from violence, exploitation, and discriminatory treatment in order to provide security and comfort;

b. that in the context of fulfilling the rights and protection of women and children from violence, exploitation, and discriminatory treatment in

Bima Regency, the role of the regional government in its implementation is required;

c. that the implementation of protection of women and children needs to be provided with direction and foundation to ensure legal certainty based on the principle of justice;

d. that based on the considerations as referred to in point a, point b, and point c, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning the Implementation of

Women Empowerment and Child Protection;

In view of : 1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;

2. Law Number 69 of 1958 concerning the Establishment of Level II Regions within the Level I Regions of Bali, West Nusa Tenggara and

East Nusa Tenggara (State Gazette of the Republic of

Indonesia of 1958 Number 122, Supplement to the State Gazette

of the Republic of Indonesia Number 1655);

3. Law Number 7 of 1984 concerning Ratification of the Convention on the Elimination of All

Forms of Discrimination Against Women (Convention on the

Elimination of All Forms Of Discrimination Against Women)

(State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1984

Number 29, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of

Indonesia Number 3277);

4. Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2002 Number 109, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4235) as amended several times, most recently by Law Number 17 of 2016 concerning Stipulation of Government Regulation in Lieu of Law Number 1 of 2016 concerning the Second Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection into Law (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2016 Number 99, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5882);

5. Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 244, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5587) as amended several times, most recently by Law

Number 9 of 2015 concerning the Second Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2015 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5679);

6. Government Regulation Number 12 of 2017 concerning Guidance and Supervision of the Implementation of Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2017 Number 73, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 6041);

7. Regulation of the Minister of Home Affairs Number 15 of 2008 concerning General Guidelines for the Implementation of Gender Mainstreaming in the Regions as amended by Regulation of the Minister of Home Affairs Number 67 of 2011 concerning Amendment to Regulation of the Minister of Home Affairs Number 15 of 2008 concerning General Guidelines for the Implementation of Gender Mainstreaming in the Regions (State

News of the Republic of Indonesia of 2011 Number 927); 8. Regulation of the Minister of Women Empowerment and Child Protection Number 4 of 2018 concerning Guidelines for the Establishment of Regional Technical Implementation Units for Women and Child Protection (State News of the Republic of Indonesia of 2018 Number 532);

9. Regional Regulation of West Nusa Tenggara Province Number 8 of 2015 concerning Implementation of Women and Child Protection (Regional Gazette of West Nusa Tenggara Province of 2015 Number 8, Supplement to the Regional Gazette of West Nusa Tenggara Province Number 119);

With the Mutual Approval of

THE REGIONAL HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES OF BIMA REGENCY

and

THE REGENT OF BIMA

DECIDES:

To enact : REGIONAL REGULATION CONCERNING THE IMPLEMENTATION OF WOMEN EMPOWERMENT AND CHILD PROTECTION.

Article 5

(1) Regional Apparatus that administers governmental affairs in the field of Women's Empowerment and Child Protection in providing services for women and children experiencing problems of violence, discrimination, special protection, and other technical problems is implemented by UPTD P3AP2KB.

(2) UPTD P3AP2KB as referred to in paragraph (1) performs service functions:

a. public complaints;
b. victim outreach;
c. case management;
d. temporary shelter;
e. mediation; and
f. victim assistance.
(3) In the implementation of service functions as referred to in paragraph (2) letter b, a task force for women's empowerment and child protection may be formed, facilitated by the Regional Apparatus responsible for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection.
(4) Service functions provided by UPTD P3AP2KB as referred to in paragraph (2) refer to service standards that have been established in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

Article 27

Provision of services for Children requiring special protection as referred to in Article 25 letter b is carried out through: a. implementation of service provision for Children requiring special protection through Regional Apparatus handling Women's Empowerment and Child Protection affairs and/or UPTD P3AP2KB in the region;

b. provision of community complaint services for Children requiring special protection in the region;

c. provision of outreach services for Children requiring special protection in the region;

d. provision of case management services for Children requiring special protection in the region;

e. provision of temporary shelter services for Children requiring special protection in the region;

f. provision of mediation services for Children requiring special protection in the region;

g. provision of assistance services for children requiring special protection in the region; and

h. provision of service facilities and infrastructure for children requiring special protection in the region.

Article 2

The implementation of women's empowerment and child protection is carried out based on the principles of:

a. respect for human rights;
b. gender equality;
c. non-discrimination;
d. victim protection;
e. best interests of the child;
f. survival and development of the child;
g. child participation; and
h. benefit.

